{
  "feature": "Swap tools v2 (sub-project 4): the stand-ins sheet from both doors, Show all, Take, the receipt, Undo swap, and the stacked stand-in",
  "clearAbout": true,
  "note": "Needs a server with SWAP_TOOLS_ENABLED=true, signed in as the swaptools-v2 account (swaptools-v2+clerk_test@example.com on local-dev, which holds Hugh's pulled HD decks), with About marked seen (every swap probe does it through clearAboutSheet). SHEET_DECK is HD - Gishath (904fdc61-e190-4ba5-8e34-2b18fa0584f2): Naya, an $8 limit, and every kind over it as a real Shopping row: Plateau (land), Wooded Foothills (fetch), Runadi, Behemoth Caller (creature) and The Great Henge (a noncreature on identity). v1's fixture was a deck probe:swap-sheet builds and deletes, so nothing durable reached the sheet, and its noncreature was Deadly Rollick, off identity. Shopping is client state: every row reaches it by a PRESS. The take, receipt and undo rows are ONE CHAIN on one page at each width, since the receipt is page state a reload loses: take writes the swap, receipt reads it, undo reverses it. A run that fails part-way through the chain leaves Runadi swapped out of HD - Gishath; undo it from the deck's Shopping list, or with probe:swap-sheet's discipline in mind, by hand.",
  "shares": {
    "module": "src/components/decks/stand-ins-sheet.tsx",
    "binding": "StandInsSheet",
    "note": "One sheet for both doors. DecklistRow's ⇄ and the card modal's StandInDoor both call openStandIns, and decklist.tsx renders the one StandInsSheet; a door that drew its own sheet is how the two would drift."
